<ns0:section xmlns:ns0="http://xml.house.gov/schemas/uslm/1.0" style="-uslm-lc:I80" id="idb8cdc10c-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8" identifier="/us/usc/t18/s497"><ns0:num value="497">§ 497.</ns0:num><ns0:heading> Letters patent</ns0:heading><ns0:content>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">Whoever falsely makes, forges, counterfeits, or alters any letters patent granted or purporting to have been granted by the President of the United States; or</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">Whoever passes, utters, or publishes, or attempts to pass, utter, or publish as genuine, any such letters patent, knowing the same to be forged, counterfeited or falsely altered—</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I11" class="indent0">Shall be fined under this title or imprisoned not more than ten years, or both.</ns0:p>
</ns0:content><ns0:sourceCredit id="idb8cdc10d-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">(<ns0:ref href="/us/act/1948-06-25/ch645">June 25, 1948, ch. 645</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/62/712">62 Stat. 712</ns0:ref>; <ns0:ref href="/us/pl/103/322/tXXXIII/s330016/1/K">Pub. L. 103–322, title XXXIII, § 330016(1)(K)</ns0:ref>, <ns0:date date="1994-09-13">Sept. 13, 1994</ns0:date>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/108/2147">108 Stat. 2147</ns0:ref>.)</ns0:sourceCredit>
<ns0:notes type="uscNote" id="idb8cdc10e-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8">
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="historicalAndRevision" id="idb8cdc10f-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Historical and Revision Notes</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Based on title 18, U.S.C., 1940 ed., § 71 (<ns0:ref href="/us/act/1909-03-04/ch321/s27">Mar. 4, 1909, ch. 321, § 27</ns0:ref>, <ns0:ref href="/us/stat/35/1094">35 Stat. 1094</ns0:ref>).</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Mandatory punishment provision was rephrased in the alternative.</ns0:p>
<ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">Changes were made in phraseology.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" role="crossHeading" topic="editorialNotes" id="idb8cdc110-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered"><ns0:b>Editorial Notes</ns0:b></ns0:heading></ns0:note>
<ns0:note style="-uslm-lc:I74" topic="amendments" id="idb8cdc111-47c4-11f1-9a61-b1559996dfe8"><ns0:heading class="centered smallCaps">Amendments</ns0:heading><ns0:p style="-uslm-lc:I21" class="indent0">1994—<ns0:ref href="/us/pl/103/322">Pub. L. 103–322</ns0:ref> substituted “fined under this title” for “fined not more than $5,000”.</ns0:p>
</ns0:note>
</ns0:notes>
</ns0:section>
